From b89aa40118e2f96cd26f1957ecfa883e04c52d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:09:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): stall notice names the LLM pacing wall
 for a pool card no worker imported

A ready card this gateway cannot lease, with no dispatch verdict (only skips saying the recording machine cannot lease it, such as the hub's labels_mismatch), got 'admission reason unknown' and the re-place advice while the pacing governor held the whole pool (t_01a1db9d9538716b; live case t_01a1db51b7673da0, ranked 62 of 66 under the import window).

- kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.paced_pools: the stall notice's read-only view of the pace this home stored (llm_pacing.json, fresh within STALE_READ_INTERVALS read intervals). It judges the card as hold() does (shared _governed, lane 'ready'), makes no usage read, writes nothing and holds nothing. Only a paced/held read for every candidate provider is positive.
- kanban_parent_unclaimed: on a positive read, admission = {reason: llm_pacing, status: held, providers: [{provider, state, until?}]}, worded like #3058's paced skip (earliest until), without the priority/re-place advice. An absent, stale, open, unknown or failing read keeps today's payload and words (fail open, BLE001 with reason).
- kanban_dispatch_skip.recorder_cannot_lease: skipped_ineligible/claim_deferred with labels_mismatch, pinned_only, held or offline is no verdict on the machines that can lease the card (allowlist; any other skip's verdict stands).
- Guard amendment per the amended card body: test_only_kanban_dispatch_consults_the_governor lists kanban_parent_unclaimed.py and pins (AST) what it takes from the governor to NOTICE_VIEW = paced_pools, admission, admission_skip; a parametrized test shows hold(), a usage read, passing the module on or a dotted import breaks the pin.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_notice_pacing_admission.py (61; 39 fail at 5f224d4d77e, 61 pass), mutation check 36/36 killed; test_kanban_llm_pacing.py 26; the 7 regression files the card names pass unmodified with its counts.
